{#- The press, for a quote made somewhere targum has no page (targum-internal#80).

    In the chat a quote becomes a card in the thread, and the card's button posts
    `/build`. Over a connector the quote is made in somebody else's app, so it comes back
    as a link to this: the same quote, the same button, the same `/build`, on a page of
    ours. `Handler._build` remains the only path to `Library.claim`, and the model still
    cannot press anything.

    It keeps the full top bar (David, 2026-10-08; design.md §12, "The connector's pages
    are the boards'", 2026-10-09; boards ConnConfirm and ConnConfirmPhone): the app's
    shell, and the board's 640px card in the column, as the subscription's confirm page
    stands. The bar adds ways off the page, never a way to press: the press is still the
    one form below, and `Handler._press` still the only road to `Library.press`.

    §6 governs the words. A wait is said in minutes and a cost in credits — one credit is
    one minute of audio or video (§12, 2026-09-23) — and never as a price: this page never
    prints what the job cost to make. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('tokens.css') }}{{ asset('shared.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('subs.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
<script>window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";</script>
</head>
<body class="press">
{% set here = 'press' %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>
<main class="sub-gate">
  <div class="card sub-confirm press-confirm">
  <p class="sub-via"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 3.5h11v7h-6l-3 2.5v-2.5h-2z"/></svg>{{ t("press.page.from-an-assistant", "From an assistant") }}</p>

  {% if job.reader %}
    {#- Already built, which is what a second visit to the same link looks like. Not an
        error, and the way on is the reader itself. -#}
    <h1 class="press-title">{{ t("press.page.this-one-is-ready", "This one is ready") }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ job.title }}</p>
    <form method="get" action="/reader/{{ job.reader }}">
      <button class="btn filled go" type="submit"><span class="go-says">{{ t("press.page.open-it", "Open it") }}</span><svg class="go-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></button>
    </form>

  {% elif job.stage in ('working', 'reading', 'queued', 'looking up words') %}
    {#- Pressed, and being made. Reached two ways: without script, where the press
        redirects back here and the way on is the button; and **with** script, where the
        reader simply reloaded or came back to the link while it built. That second way
        used to dead-end — the watcher looked for the press form, which this state has
        not got, so the page never polled and never opened the reader (2026-09-23). The
        watch hangs off its own element, present in both states, so coming back to the
        tab is the same as never having left it.

        `queued` and `looking up words` are waits too, and fell to the refusal below:
        every press without script landed on "We can't make this one" while the build
        was on its way (copy audit, 2026-09-28). A quote still being costed says so. -#}
    <h1 class="press-title">{{ t("press.page.we-re-making-it", "We're making it") }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ job.title }}</p>
    <div id="press-watch" data-job="{{ job.id }}" data-made="{{ job.made|int }}"
         data-usually="{{ job.usually|round|int }}"></div>
    <p class="said" id="press-doing" role="status">{%- if job.stage == 'looking up words' %}{{ t("press.page.working-out-how-long", "We're working out how long it'll take.") }}{% else %}{{ job.message or t("press.page.getting-started", "We're getting it ready.") }}{% endif %}</p>
    <p class="said" id="press-left" role="status"></p>
    <form method="get" action="/build/{{ job.id }}">
      <button class="btn filled go" type="submit">{{ t("press.page.see-how-it-s-going", "See how it's going") }}</button>
    </form>
    <p class="aside">{{ t("press.page.close-find-it-in-your-targums", "You can close this page. You'll find it in Your targums.") }}
      <a href="/">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-targums", "Go to Your targums") }}</a></p>

  {% elif job.stage == 'ready' %}
    {#- The board's card (ConnConfirm): what it is over its title, the English under it,
        how long until it is ready and in how many parts, then a hairline, what it uses
        with what the month has left, and Confirm. -#}
    {%- set minutes = ((job.seconds or 0) / 60)|round|int %}
    {%- if job.audio and minutes %}
    <p class="press-kicker">{{ t("library.minutes", "{n} min", n=minutes) }}{% if job.known_line %} · {{ job.known_line }}{% endif %}</p>
    {%- elif job.known_line %}
    <p class="press-kicker">{{ job.known_line }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <h1 class="press-title" dir="auto">{{ job.title }}</h1>
    {%- if job.english %}<p class="press-english">{{ job.english }}</p>{% endif %}
    <ul class="press-facts">
      {#- `usually` is seconds — `Library._how_long` says so. It was rendered as minutes
          here, which promised "about 420 minutes" for a seven-minute build. The quote's
          guess is put away the moment the press lands, because from then on the page is
          watching this build and can say something truer (2026-09-23). -#}
      {%- if job.usually and job.usually >= 30 %}
      <li id="press-quoted"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="5.75"/><path d="M8 5v3.25l2 1.25"/></svg>{{ tn("press.page.ready-in-about-minutes", (job.usually / 60)|round|int, "Ready in about {n} minute", "Ready in about {n} minutes") }}</li>
      {%- endif %}
      {#- One press gets the whole of it (David, 2026-10-07; design.md §12, "One press gets
          the whole video, a part at a time"), so the page says how it arrives. -#}
      {%- if job.audio and job.parts and job.parts > 1 %}
      <li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 4.5h8M2.5 8h8M2.5 11.5h5M11.5 9.5v4l2.5-2z"/></svg>{{ tn("press.page.in-parts", job.parts, "In {n} part, each made as you reach it", "In {n} parts, each made as you reach it") }}</li>
      {%- endif %}
    </ul>
    <div class="press-foot">
      <p class="press-cost">
        {%- if job.audio %}
        {#- A cost is credits since 2026-09-23 (§12), a credit a minute of audio or video;
            the month's balance beside it, with the time it comes to. -#}
        <b>{{ tn("press.page.uses-credits", minutes, "Uses {n} credit", "Uses {n} credits") }}</b>
        {%- if credits.left is not none and credits.left is defined %}
        <span>{{ tn("press.page.left-this-month", credits.left, "{n} left this month · about {clock} of audio", "{n} left this month · about {clock} of audio", clock=clock) }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- else %}
        <b>{{ t("press.page.uses-no-credits", "Reading it uses no credits") }}</b>
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
      <div class="press-acts">
        {#- Not now presses nothing: it goes to Your targums, and the quote waits. -#}
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/">{{ t("connect.page.not-now", "Not now") }}</a>
        <form method="post" action="/build/{{ job.id }}" id="press" data-job="{{ job.id }}"
              data-usually="{{ job.usually|round|int }}">
          <button class="btn filled go" type="submit"><span class="go-says">{{ t("press.page.confirm", "Confirm") }}</span></button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="said" id="press-doing" role="status" hidden></p>
    <p class="said" id="press-left" role="status" hidden></p>
    {#- Said before the press, and replaced by the way out once it is pressed: until then
        "go to your texts" would be pointing at a text that is not there. -#}
    <p class="aside" id="press-note">{{ t("press.page.you-asked-for-this-somewhere-else", "You asked for this somewhere else. Nothing has been made yet.") }}</p>
    <p class="aside" id="press-away" hidden>{{ t("press.page.close-find-it-in-your-targums", "You can close this page. You'll find it in Your targums.") }}
      <a href="/">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-targums", "Go to Your targums") }}</a></p>

  {% else %}
    <h1 class="press-title">{{ t("press.page.we-can-t-make-this-one", "We can't make this one") }}</h1>
    {%- if job.act == 'plan' and job.blocked and not job.error %}
    {#- A free reader out of credits, offered the plan in place (design.md §12, "A free
        reader meets the plan where they reach for it", 2026-10-09). -#}
    {%- set upgrade_said = job.blocked %}{% set upgrade_fact = job.fact %}
    {% include '_upgrade.html.j2' %}
    {%- else %}
    <p class="said">{{ job.error or job.blocked or t("press.page.that-quote-has-gone-stale", "We couldn't get this one ready. Ask for it again where you asked before.") }}</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="aside"><a href="/">{{ t("press.page.go-to-your-targums", "Go to Your targums") }}</a></p>
  {% endif %}
  </div>
</main>
{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}
<script>window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in names %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };</script>
{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('press.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
